<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip Francis Little</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1824–1897</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip Francis Little was a lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-edward-island">Prince Edward Island</a> who became the first premier of the Colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> when responsible government was introduced in 1855. Leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a>, which drew strong support from Irish Catholics, he served until 1858 and later became a judge of Newfoundland's Supreme Court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-francis-little.jpg" alt="Philip Francis Little" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_Francis_Little.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
